14
01:02:05,217 --> 01:02:11,217
Off Limits is a 1988 action-thriller film set during the Vietnam War starring
Willem Dafoe and Gregory Hines and directed by Christopher Crowe.

15
01:06:31,304 --> 01:06:37,304
The term "off limits" referred to the area where the original crime took
place, an area of Saigon off limits to military personnel.

16
01:10:57,391 --> 01:11:03,391
The name of the film was changed to Saigon or Saigon: Off Limits
when it was released throughout the rest of the world.

17
01:15:23,478 --> 01:15:29,478
The film marks Willem Dafoe's second Vietnam War film.

18
01:19:49,565 --> 01:19:55,565
He was assisted in preparing for this role by Vietnam Veteran and
former Counterintelligence Special Agent Ed Murphy.

19
01:24:15,652 --> 01:24:21,652
Dafoe had previously starred in Platoon and would go on to play roles in
Born on the Fourth of July and Flight of the Intruder.

20
01:28:41,739 --> 01:28:47,739
Although set during the war, the tale is more of a
mystery than a story about the war.

21
01:33:07,826 --> 01:33:13,826
The film explores themes of helicopter, undercover, racism, prostitution.

22
01:37:33,913 --> 01:37:39,913
The tone is intense and emotional and mind_bending.
